text:
julia: Trying to import the TS SDK in an Expo-managed app (Hermes) and it crashes: crypto.getRandomValues is not a function. Minimal repro attached.
maria: Hermes doesn't have WebCrypto. You need a RN polyfill like react-native-get-random-values and Buffer. Make sure it runs before any SDK imports.
julia: I put import 'react-native-get-random-values' at top of App.tsx but crash happens inside node_modules/@redwood/sdk/dist/index.mjs during module evaluation. Shim isn't running soon enough.
kevin: Metro/expo sometimes resolves .mjs/module fields and evaluates packages earlier. Two paths: 1) set a shim as the Expo entryPoint so it executes before the app bundle; 2) we should publish a CJS/react-native entry so Metro prefers that build.
maria: Also RN's fetch doesn't supply ReadableStream. If the SDK expects streaming (getReader/pipeTo) it will fail. SDK should detect RN and fallback to arrayBuffer()/text() and emit non-streamed responses or simulated chunks.
julia: That explains why chat streaming doesn't work for meI only get the full body at the end.
maria: Quick shim to try:
// shim.js
import 'react-native-get-random-values';
import { Buffer } from 'buffer';
global.Buffer = Buffer;
if (!global.crypto) global.crypto = { getRandomValues: require('react-native-get-random-values').getRandomValues };
Then set app.json: { "expo": { "entryPoint": "./shim.js" } }
kevin: On the SDK side we should: publish a cjs/react-native entry, add runtime detection for RN, widen TypeScript response types to ReadableStream | ArrayBuffer | string, and provide a sample expo template.
julia: Another bug: auth refresh + retry on 401 causes duplicate POSTs on mobile because fetch isn't abortable and our retry wrapper replays requests. Repro: expired token -> request 401 -> refresh + replay -> concurrent requests duplicate.
maria: Fix is singleflight token refresh (one refresh promise others await) and make autoretry opt-in on mobile or add small dedupe window. I can prototype a mutex around refresh and add tests simulating RN fetch behavior (no streams, no abort).
kevin: I'll open an SDK issue to add: RN entrypoint, streaming fallback, typings update, and singleflight auth refresh. infra-bot: Issue created #1355: expo-hermes: shim + cjs entry + streaming fallback + auth-singleflight. Assignee: kevin.
julia: Thanks, I'll try the shim + entryPoint change and share repro if it works.
